jobs.description:
Experience in the United States Navy in as a Post-Command Commander afloat or equivalent.
Five years’ experience on Echelon 3 or higher staff.
Five years’ experience in database design and management;
Five years’ experience in data analysis for complex projects;
Experience with analyzing specific metrics embedded within the PESTONI (Personnel, Equipment, Supply, Training, Ordnance, Infrastructure/Networks) pillars of analysis;
Ability to develop a comprehensive understanding of the Surface Force’s business practices, primary (organic) data sources, secondary(non-organic) data needs, data gaps, and organic analytic capabilities to inform the development of a meaningful data visualization tool suite and predictive modeling needs for decision-makers at all levels;
Demonstrated experience developing and applying machine learning models, predictive analytics, and AI-driven data interpretation to complex defense problems;
Proficiency in leveraging modern data analytics platforms and languages (e.g., Python, R) to perform statistical analysis and build financial and operational risk models;
Highly proficient and experienced with Microsoft Office, especially with Access, Excel and PowerPoint;
Experience in producing executive-level analytical products and reports;
Master’s degree (or higher) from an accredited college or university (a major in an Analytics or Computer related field is highly desired).
Secret security clearance required.

